# AQP UI

- `aqp_ui/` is the **customer-facing**, cloud-hosted Next.js 14+ App
  Router frontend serving both B2B (Entra ID + `EntraTenantLink`) and
  B2C (Auth0 Organizations) customers. It is NOT the local operator UI
  (`aqp_client/`) and NOT the internal admin (`aqp_admin/`).
- **Never import `aqp.*` or `aqp_control_plane.*`.** HTTP-only access
  to the AQP monolith (`AQP_API_BASE`) and the control plane
  (`AQP_CONTROL_PLANE_URL`). Types come from `src/lib/api/generated/`
  (run `pnpm gen:api`).
- **Identity** flows through the existing
  [IdentityProvider](mdc:aqp/auth/providers/protocol.py) chain (AQP
  rule 27). `aqp_ui` mints PKCE state, holds the unified JWE session
  cookie, and forwards the access token via `Authorization: Bearer`.
  Vendor SDKs (`@auth0/nextjs-auth0`, `@azure/msal-node`) MAY appear
  only under `src/lib/auth/` and `src/app/api/auth/*`.
- **Credentials** resolve through env-only variables synced by
  External Secrets Operator from HashiCorp Vault. Never embed secrets
  in client bundles. Never print tokens or kubeconfigs (always-on rule
  [aqp-management-engine.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/aqp-management-engine.mdc)).
- **Multi-tenancy**: every `/api/*` handler reads
  `getSession()` from `src/lib/auth/session.ts`, extracts active
  `org_id` / `workspace_id` / `project_id` / `lab_id` / `mode` claims,
  and attaches `X-AQP-Org` / `X-AQP-Workspace` / `X-AQP-Project` /
  `X-AQP-Lab` / `X-AQP-Mode` headers via `src/lib/api/tenancy.ts`.
  Mirrors [aqp_client/src/lib/api/client.ts](mdc:aqp_client/src/lib/api/client.ts).
- **Step-up MFA (RFC 9470)**: every BFF handler proxying a
  step-up-gated upstream endpoint MUST bubble
  `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer error="insufficient_user_authentication"`
  back to the client unchanged. The client retries through
  `src/hooks/useStepUp.ts`.
- **Kill-switch fan-out**: `POST /api/kill-switch` fans out via
  `Promise.allSettled` to `/portfolio/kill_switch`, `/agents/halt`,
  `/paper/stop-all`, `/bots/halt-all`, `/rl/halt-all`,
  `/workflows/halt`. Matches the existing
  [KillSwitch.tsx](mdc:aqp_client/src/components/common/KillSwitch.tsx).
- **EntityPicker** for every name/credential selection. Free-text is
  reserved for descriptions and queries, never for the names of
  datasets, namespaces, sink kinds, Airbyte connectors, projects,
  credentials, broker credentials, etc. Use
  `src/components/common/EntityPicker.tsx`.
- **WebSocket frames** preserve `{task_id, stage, message, timestamp,
  **extras}` per AQP rule 4.
- **CVE-2025-29927 pinning**: Next.js pinned to `>=14.2.25`. NEVER
  rely solely on `middleware.ts` for auth — every route handler MUST
  re-check the session via `getSession()`.

## Where changes go

| Change | Location |
| --- | --- |
| Marketing page | `aqp_ui/src/app/(marketing)/<slug>/page.tsx` |
| Auth screen | `aqp_ui/src/app/(auth)/<slug>/page.tsx` |
| Protected dashboard page | `aqp_ui/src/app/(app)/<slug>/page.tsx` |
| BFF route handler | `aqp_ui/src/app/api/<area>/route.ts` |
| Unified session interface | `aqp_ui/src/lib/auth/session.ts` |
| Typed HTTP client | `aqp_ui/src/lib/api/client.ts` |
| Tenancy header builder | `aqp_ui/src/lib/api/tenancy.ts` |
| Shared UI primitive | `aqp_ui/src/components/common/` |
| Theme tokens | `aqp_ui/src/providers/AntdProvider.tsx` |

## Validation

```bash
cd aqp_ui
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
pnpm test
pnpm build

# Boundary guard: must return nothing.
rg --type ts --type tsx "from ['\"]@aqp/" src
rg --type ts --type tsx "from ['\"]\.\./\.\./aqp" src
```

Consider these rules if they affect your changes.
